People would stand in amazement as these heroic horse-drawn machines sped through the streets.

115
00:11:26,260 --> 00:11:30,180
Fire dogs ran with the horses and guarded them at the fire scene.

116
00:11:31,900 --> 00:11:37,920
Most fire dogs were Dalmatians because they possessed a unique ability to get along with horses.

117
00:11:37,921 --> 00:11:51,820
steam engines could stop a fire from destroying an entire town if they arrived in time often though

118
00:11:51,821 --> 00:11:58,660
they did not somebody had to go run to a fire station then somebody had to go run from the

119
00:11:58,661 --> 00:12:03,300
fire station and go find the firefighters if they were volunteers have them come back they would get

120
00:12:03,301 --> 00:12:09,800
the piece of apparatus and then go to the fire. There was a significant delay.

121
00:12:09,801 --> 00:12:16,800
It also took time to connect an engine to the closest water supply.

122
00:12:16,801 --> 00:12:25,300
This delay gave rise to another invention, the soda acid fire extinguisher.

123
00:12:25,301 --> 00:12:32,800
By creating a controlled chemical reaction, soda acid extinguishers provided an instant source of pressurized water.

124
00:12:32,801 --> 00:12:33,501
water.

125
00:12:33,502 --> 00:12:39,800
The extinguisher was filled with soda water, a solution of water and sodium bicarbonate.

126
00:12:42,860 --> 00:12:46,201
On top was a capsule of hydrochloric acid.

127
00:12:46,202 --> 00:12:49,860
At a fire the two were mixed, generating large

128
00:12:50,360 --> 00:12:55,081
amounts of carbon dioxide gas, which pushed the water out.

129
00:12:55,082 --> 00:12:57,360
Soda acid extinguishers were

130
00:12:57,361 --> 00:13:04,360
Soda acid extinguishers were a vital component of a successful fire attack.

131
00:13:04,361 --> 00:13:11,360
They could easily tackle small fires and delay the spread of bigger fires until the steam engine was ready for action.

132
00:13:11,361 --> 00:13:17,360
By the late 1800's firefighting had become a profession.

133
00:13:17,361 --> 00:13:25,360
Most cities developed a core of expertly trained men who were strategically placed in firehouses around town.

134
00:13:25,361 --> 00:13:34,280
To ensure a speedy response, alarm boxes began to appear at nearly every street corner in the 1850s

135
00:13:34,281 --> 00:13:39,200
They were connected to the firehouse by telegraph

136
00:13:39,201 --> 00:13:44,960
The person would go up and he would open up the box and pull the lever inside the fire alarm box

137
00:13:44,961 --> 00:13:48,580
That would transmit the signal down to here

138
00:13:48,581 --> 00:13:50,360
It would punch this paper tape

139
00:13:50,361 --> 00:13:54,700
In this case it would be like 2217

140
